# __PROJECT_NAME__

A [Maximus](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus) service on Cloudflare Workers: an API whose routes are
files, served to agents as MCP tools when they say so, and configured in one file, `vite.config.ts`.

## Start

```sh
bun install
bun run dev
```

`bun run dev` serves the Worker at `http://localhost:5173`. `GET /api/v1/greeting` answers
`{ "message": "Hello World" }` to a signed-in caller. Locally, the development token in `.dev.vars` signs you
in, from localhost alone:

```sh
curl -H "authorization: Bearer $(cut -d= -f2 .dev.vars)" http://localhost:5173/api/v1/greeting
```

`/api/openapi.json` describes the API, and `/health` answers without a token.

## Build on it

| To add                      | Do                                                                               |
| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| A route                     | `bunx maximus gen route get '/v1/tasks/{taskId}'` writes its file in `routes/`   |
| A tool only agents call     | `bunx maximus gen tool summarize-tasks` writes `mcp/tools/summarize-tasks.ts`    |
| A binding (KV, D1, R2, …)   | `env: { TASKS: bindings.kv() }` in `maximus()`, with `bindings` from `cf/config` |
| Your own failures           | `errors.ts` default-exports `defineErrors({ … })`                                |
| A provider's webhook        | `pages/webhooks/<provider>.post.ts`, which verifies the delivery's signature     |
| Observers or analytics      | `telemetry.ts` default-exports `defineTelemetry({ observers })`                  |
| What every handler receives | `context.ts` default-exports `defineContext(…)`                                  |

`bun install`, `vp dev`, `vp test` and `vp build` generate `.maximus/` from these files; never edit it.
[Project structure](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus/blob/main/docs/guides/project-structure.md)
maps every file and folder a project can hold.

## Test, verify and deploy

`bun run test` runs the tests in `tests/` in Node, and `bun run verify` runs the types, lint and format,
the tests and the build. Before the first deployment, set `origin` in `vite.config.ts` to the Worker's
HTTPS URL (its workers.dev URL or a custom domain you own) and `tokens.issuer` to your authorization server.
Then:

```sh
bunx cf auth login
bun run deploy
```

The GitHub workflow verifies every pull request and deploys `main`, given the repository secrets
`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`. The
[Maximus documentation](https://github.com/getarbol/maximus/blob/main/docs/README.md) covers the rest.
